weighing in at 200,000 kilos and  stretching the length of a basketball  court  the blue whale tops the big animal  charts now researchers think the  seasonal availability of its forty  million krill a day diet may have led to  their behemoth size what does the fossil  record say researchers knew from living  whale proportions that the size of a  whale correlates with the width of its  cheek bones they then measured skulls of  63 extinct whale species and 13 modern  species and plotted them on a timeline  that showed the whale family tree  the whales didn't get to be really big  early on nor did they gradually get  bigger over time instead they became  moderately large and stayed that way  until about 4.5 million years ago then  baleen whales went from relatively big  to ginormous 4.5 million years ago the  biggest whales were only ten meters long  today  blue whales are 30 meters what was  happening 4.5 million years ago it was  the beginning of the first ice ages and  as glaciers expanded spring and summer  runoff poured lots of nutrients into the  coastal ocean fueling explosive growth  of whale food that seasonal runoff  created a new pattern of food  availability seasonal patches very  abundant food spaced far apart for the  course of the year why would that make  for bigger whales modern whale studies  show that the more concentrated the food  the greater the feeding efficiency  especially in whales with really big  mouths furthermore larger whales can  travel faster between patches of prey so  baleen whales that got  bigger faster thrived while smaller  species went extinct so for whale  evolution it's not quite you are what  you eat but close  [Music]
 

